---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About — Aravind Anilraj (phi5ic)"
  description="Systems engineer and Linux contributor. Research in erasure coding, distributed consensus, and Linux kernel internals."
>
  <div class="space-y-10 font-mono">
    <!-- Header -->
    <header class="border border-[#2a0e2e] bg-[#100613] p-4 sm:p-5 rounded-sm space-y-1">
      <div class="text-[11px] text-[#854d80]">phi5ic@mesh ~ $ man aravind</div>
      <h1 class="text-lg sm:text-xl font-bold text-white tracking-tight flex items-center gap-2">
        <span>About / Identity</span>
        <span class="text-[#ff2a85] text-xs font-normal">[phi5ic]</span>
      </h1>
      <p class="text-xs text-[#c9a6c5]">
        Systems engineering, Linux kernel internals, and distributed storage research.
      </p>
    </header>

    <!-- Bio Statement -->
    <section class="space-y-3 text-xs sm:text-sm text-[#ecd2e8] leading-relaxed border-l-2 border-[#ff2a85] pl-4">
      <p>
        I'm <strong>Aravind Anilraj</strong> (<code>phi5ic</code>). I'm a systems engineer and open-source Linux kernel contributor.
      </p>
      <p>
        I think the best way to understand systems is to dive into the deep end without prerequisites and see what breaks. I hate repetitive college lectures and exams, so I spend my time building filesystems, hacking on kernel drivers, and wrestling with distributed consensus math.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- Research & Interests -->
    <section class="space-y-3">
      <div class="border-b border-[#2a0e2e] pb-1.5">
        <h2 class="text-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-[#ff2a85] font-bold">
          -- [01] RESEARCH &amp; INTERESTS --
        </h2>
      </div>
      <ul class="space-y-2 text-xs sm:text-sm text-[#ecd2e8]">
        <li>
          <strong class="text-white">&gt; Storage Architecture &amp; Coding Theory:</strong> Erasure coding, binary MDS array codes (EVENODD, RDP, Liberation, STAR), sub-packet slice repair, and write-amplification bounds.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong class="text-white">&gt; Distributed Systems:</strong> Virtual consensus meshes, decentralized Raft state replication, and fast fault recovery without centralized metadata.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong class="text-white">&gt; Operating Systems &amp; Kernel Internals:</strong> Upstream Linux kernel contributions (ASoC sound, Thermal), userspace subsystems, and FUSE filesystems.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong class="text-white">&gt; Computer Arithmetic:</strong> SIMD vectorization, finite-field arithmetic over GF(2ᵐ), and cryptographic homology graph verification.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <!-- Projects -->
    <section class="space-y-3">
      <div class="flex items-center justify-between border-b border-[#2a0e2e] pb-1.5">
        <h2 class="text-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-[#ff2a85] font-bold">
          -- [02] WORKBENCH --
        </h2>
        <a href="/projects/" class="text-xs text-[#ff79c6] hover:underline no-underline">[all projects &rarr;]</a>
      </div>
      <ul class="space-y-2.5 text-xs sm:text-sm text-[#ecd2e8]">
        <li>
          <strong class="text-white">&bull; Nifsi:</strong> Distributed userspace OS on Linux (<a href="https://github.com/phi5ic/Nifsi" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-[#ff2a85] hover:text-[#ff79c6]">github.com/phi5ic/Nifsi &nearr;</a>).
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong class="text-white">&bull; Linux Kernel Patches:</strong> 6 upstream patches merged into Linux across ASoC sound and Thermal int340x (<a href="/patches/" class="text-[#ff2a85] hover:text-[#ff79c6]">view patches &rarr;</a>). Reviewed by Mark Brown and Rafael J. Wysocki.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong class="text-white">&bull; StabiSense:</strong> Dynamic chipset stabilization system for silicon manufacturing, presented at IEEE Thailand 2026.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong class="text-white">&bull; Qgis-Simulation:</strong> Satellite radar pipeline breach detection (1st Place Flowvision Hackathon).
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

